issue.body:
Active downstream gate after #245 `FULL_CHARACTER_MODEL_LOCK_R02 = PASS`.

Purpose: prove how the already-defined ZORR ivory suit deforms under a small set of real pose forces without redesigning the character or turning the sheet into realism study.

Authority inputs:
- accepted suit turnaround;
- accepted costume/accessory sheet;
- `BODY_CONSTRUCTION_R01`;
- `HANDS_CANON_R03` / `HAND_EXPRESSION_R01` for cuff/watch interaction;
- current ZORR fold law: folds only where force requires; ivory remains calm; 2–5 meaningful fold shapes per large garment region.

Target high-information controls:
1. shoulder/arm raise — shoulder seam + armpit tension;
2. elbow bend — sleeve compression + cuff/watch;
3. torso twist — lapel/chest/waist relationship;
4. seated hip/waist compression — jacket hem + trouser waist/crotch;
5. knee bend — trouser knee compression/tension;
6. stride/ankle — trouser break + shoe relation.

Hard law: anime readability and large graphic garment planes outrank realistic cloth simulation. No decorative wrinkle noise.

No image generation/editing is authorized by this tracker. Visual execution requires separate OWNER authorization under current image rule.

Terminal goal: `COSTUME_MECHANICS_R01 = PASS` when attachment anchors stay invariant, force-driven folds are repeatable, silhouette remains fashion-first, and no hidden costume redesign appears.
